  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "The area of the region bounded by the curve $y=x^3$ its tangent at (1,1) and X-axis is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "NfLCR",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{12} \\mathrm{sq}$ unit",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "HD4j9",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{6} \\mathrm{sq}$ unit",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Kx00Y",
      "text": "$\\frac{2}{17} \\mathrm{sq}$ unit",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "P4eeG",
      "text": "$\\frac{2}{15} \\mathrm{sq}$ unit",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "We have, $y=x^{3}$ and $A(1,1)$\r\n$\\therefore$ $\\frac{d y}{d x}=3 x^{2}$\r\nOn putting $x=1$ in $\\mathrm{Eq}$. $\\frac{d y}{d x}=3(1)^{2}=3$\r\n$\\therefore$ Equation of tangent at $A(1,1)$ is\r\n$y-1=3(x-1) \\Rightarrow y=3 x-2$\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/2015_mat_a111.png\">\r\n\r\n$\\therefore$ Required area $=\\int_{0}^{1} x^{3} d x-\\int_{2 / 3}^{1}(3 x-2) d x$\r\n$=\\left[\\frac{x^{4}}{4}\\right]_{0}^{1}-\\left[\\frac{3 x^{2}}{2}-2 x\\right]_{2 / 3}^{1}$\r\n$=\\frac{1}{4}-\\left[\\left(\\frac{3}{2}-2\\right)-\\left(\\frac{2}{3}-\\frac{4}{3}\\right)\\right]$\r\n$=\\frac{1}{12} \\mathrm{sq}$ unit",
    "image": null
  },
